From 63a21090137172589ece80017c95d5302f5bb2e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 10:02:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09320/11362] Correct the v37 prep status: the package is
 ready, the script's poll was short

The prep script exited with save_run='?' and parquet=MISSING, so the file recorded
ready_for_operator_submit=false. That is the script's own short-poll artifact -- its wait
is shorter than this kernel's runtime, the same false alarm recorded against v9, v22 and
v27 in this file's own history.

Ground truth, checked by hand: kernel status COMPLETE, and `kaggle kernels output` returns
submission.parquet at 2648 bytes, one row by four columns. The same run validated the full
scored stack -- vLLM server up in 425s, admission exact at max_model_len 155472, 8 of 8
concurrent requests round-tripped through the llama.cpp response translation, server config
max_num_seqs 8, AOT cache staged, CUDA 13 toolchain resolved.

Prepared only. Submitting remains operator-only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
---
 ops/arc-daily-prep-status.json | 14 +++++++-------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ops/arc-daily-prep-status.json b/ops/arc-daily-prep-status.json
index 98250ad8f8..27a39ea5bf 100644
